7) What is DOM?

- DOM means Document Object Model.
- It is a Programming interface for a Web Document.
- It represents HTML elements as a tree structure ( nodes ).
- With DOM we can Add, Update and Delete elements dynamically.

--> 4 Important Properties of DOM Elements :

i) innerHTML :
- Gets or Sets HTML content (Including Tags)

ii) innerText :
- Gets or Sets only the text (Ignores Tags, Respects CSS Visibility)

iii) TextContent :
- Returns the name of the HTML tag (Like div,h1 etc.)

--> Ways To Access Elements :

i) getElementById('id') :
- Select an Element by it's ID.

ii) getElementByClassName('class') :
- Select an Element by it's Class.

iii) querySelector('selector') :
- Select First matching element (CSS Selector)

iv) querySelectorAll('selector') :
- Select all matching elements (NodeList)





8) Difference Between Pseudo Element and Pseudo Class?

- Pseudo Element : It is Used to Target a specific part of an Element.
- Psedo Class : It is used to Target state of an Element.

- Pseudo Element : Here we use :: .
- Pseudo Class : Here we use : .

- Pseudo Element : ::first-line, ::first-letter, ::before, ::after
- Pseudo Class : :hover, :focus, :link, :active, :visited





